      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159695",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X = [X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}]^{T}$ be a multivariate normal random vector with mean vector $\u03bc$ and covariance matrix $\u03a3$ given by\n$\u03bc = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, \u03a3 = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nLet $Y = X_{1} + 2X_{2} - X_{3}$. Find $P(Y < 1)$.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\u03a6(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $0.05$ | $0.06$ | $0.07$ | $0.08$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0.5$ | $0.7088$ | $0.7123$ | $0.7157$ | $0.7190$ |\n| $0.6$ | $0.7422$ | $0.7454$ | $0.7486$ | $0.7517$ |\n| $0.7$ | $0.7734$ | $0.7764$ | $0.7794$ | $0.7823$ |\n| $0.8$ | $0.8023$ | $0.8051$ | $0.8078$ | $0.8106$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
